5,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I think we should look into administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as depot supervisors and the last rollout, to see how our staff handles these transitions.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'll go with the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover, plus the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial. We need to know if the gear actually works on the floor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I will examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests and the five years of renewal invoices to understand the long-term cost patterns.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I'll check the support ownership during last winter's outage and the warehouse rule changes after new accounts. I want to see who takes responsibility when things go wrong.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I'll investigate the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move to assess our history with technical debt and external migrations.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,pass,Misaki,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, do you think the warehouse rule changes will tell us if the new system needs to be more flexible for the depot crews?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,pass,Toshio,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, exactly. I'm worried that if the system is too rigid, it'll just stop matching our actual business needs within a few months.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"That is a valid concern, Yumi. I suspect my look into the 2018 data lift might reveal similar issues regarding how external plans translate into our daily operational reality.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,pass,Misaki,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that makes sense. I just hope we don't end up with another tool that everyone ignores in favor of their own spreadsheets.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,pass,Toshio,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, that's why I'm looking at the outage support. If the tools are ignored or broken, we need to know exactly who is responsible for fixing them.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. Clarity on accountability is often the difference between a minor glitch and a total operational standstill.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with all of you. It seems we have covered the financial, technical, and human elements of the transition. I am satisfied with our selections for this round.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Kenji,,Me too. Let's see what we find out.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
