35,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,It seems we are in a precarious position with our staffing; we have key administrators retiring and a very difficult time filling those specialized roles.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"That's worrying, but the floor is just as messy. Our peak season is a total blackout for cutovers, and our current yard hardware is a mismatched disaster that doesn't play well with general tools.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The financial side is equally concerning; the board is cutting capital budgets while operating costs slide through, and bundled pricing is the only thing that has remained stable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found that our support is scattered across too many vendors, leading to finger-pointing during outages, and our warehouse rules change far too often for a frozen project scope to survive.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"To add to that, our technical history is plagued by skipped upgrades due to testing constraints and a botched external data migration that left us with errors for a year.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if the warehouse rules change that quickly, we can't afford a rigid implementation, especially since we lack the administrators to fix it ourselves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, exactly. If the system can't handle the actual yard conditions and our peak-season chaos, it doesn't matter how the administrators feel; the depot will just stop using it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, given the history of skipped upgrades and botched migrations, we must be wary of any solution that requires frequent, complex updates or heavy reliance on external data lifts.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree. And if we have multiple vendors for one system, we'll just repeat that finger-pointing we saw during the winter outage. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are all converging on the same fear: a fragmented system that is too rigid to adapt and too complex to maintain with our dwindling internal expertise.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, precisely. We need a vendor that provides comprehensive training and a deployment model that doesn't rely on a few overworked people who might retire tomorrow.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"And we need someone who understands that the depot doesn't stop for a software update. If the vendor can't handle a non-freeze window during peak season, they aren't the right fit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I also want to avoid a pricing model where costs creep up through separate licenses. A bundled, predictable cost structure is essential if we are to keep the board's approval.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that makes sense. If we combine that with a single point of support, we can avoid both the financial surprises and the operational chaos we've been seeing.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,It appears we are looking for a partner who offers a unified suite with a stable cost structure and a deployment strategy that respects our operational constraints.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I believe we should prioritize a vendor that can provide on-site support or a very strong training partner to ensure the depot supervisors actually adopt the system.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree. If the trainers just visit for a week and leave, the supervisors will just go back to their old ways the moment they walk out the door.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will be looking for a vendor that avoids the trap of separate, escalating licenses. A fixed or bundled cost is the only way to ensure long-term viability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'll be looking for a vendor that offers a single, hosted suite to eliminate the finger-pointing and ensure the system can evolve with our warehouse rules.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will prioritize a solution that minimizes the risk of technical debt and avoids the pitfalls of poorly managed external migrations.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
