61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the candidates, Anchor Industrial Software seems strongest because they provide an engineering team through rollout, which addresses our staffing gaps and supervisor adoption issues.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Misaki. Anchor's focus on transport operators and having a team on-site should help them handle our yard hardware and the peak-season chaos better than a general cloud suite.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"I am concerned about Anchor's on-premise model, but Meridian Systems offers a hosted suite with a fixed configuration, which suggests the predictable cost structure I am looking for.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, Meridian's hosted suite is appealing for accountability, but a fixed configuration might be too rigid for our warehouse rules. Tessera's configurable workflows seem like a safer bet for flexibility.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Tessera's partner-led migration is a risk given our history, but Corvus's modular licensing is a nightmare for costs. I lean toward Anchor for the stability of having engineers on-site to prevent technical debt.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, while Tessera is flexible, a partner firm handling training might not be enough to stop our supervisors from reverting to old habits. Anchor's engineering team is a more permanent safety net.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, if Anchor's team is on-site, they can actually see the yard devices and the peak-season madness. That's way more valuable than a fixed configuration that might not even work for us.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, that is a fair point. However, Anchor's on-premise deployment means we bear the long-term maintenance burden, which is risky given our administrator retirements. Meridian's hosted model removes that specific worry.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, but Meridian's fixed configuration is exactly the kind of rigidity that fails when our warehouse rules change. We need a system that can adapt, or we'll be back to spreadsheets.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, you're right about the rigidity. If we choose Meridian, we risk a system that is obsolete within a year. Anchor's on-site presence mitigates the maintenance risk by ensuring it's built correctly from the start.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, if we have Anchor's engineers during the rollout, they can document everything and train the remaining staff properly, reducing the risk of the knowledge gap after retirements.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I'm sold on Anchor. Having people here who actually understand transport is the only way we survive the next peak season without a total meltdown.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I see your points. If the on-site team can guarantee a stable transition and the costs are managed, Anchor's industry focus outweighs the benefits of a hosted suite. I can support Anchor.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree. While I wanted a hosted suite for accountability, Anchor's on-site engineering team provides a different kind of accountability—they can't point fingers when they are standing right here in our warehouse.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a consensus. Anchor Industrial Software addresses our operational constraints, staffing shortages, and technical risks more effectively than the other candidates. I vote for Anchor.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
